WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.600
How can one little column change an answer by thousands?

00:00:04.250 --> 00:00:07.641
Today we are using written addition and subtraction.

00:00:07.861 --> 00:00:14.080
We will line up equal place values and see how regrouping changes the grouping without changing the amount.

00:00:14.300 --> 00:00:17.112
What happens when a column contains zero?

00:00:17.762 --> 00:00:22.937
Our learning goal is to add and subtract whole numbers accurately using written methods.

00:00:23.587 --> 00:00:25.346
Success criteria.

00:00:25.566 --> 00:00:27.991
I can line up matching place values.

00:00:28.211 --> 00:00:30.661
I can regroup without changing the total.

00:00:30.881 --> 00:00:33.559
I can check subtraction by adding back.

00:00:34.209 --> 00:00:37.272
Keep ones under ones and tens under tens.

00:00:37.492 --> 00:00:42.394
Ten units in any column can be exchanged for one unit in the column to its left.

00:00:42.614 --> 00:00:47.218
In subtraction we can exchange one larger unit for ten smaller units.

00:00:47.868 --> 00:00:53.197
Add two thousand seven hundred and eighty-six and one thousand four hundred and fifty-seven.

00:00:53.417 --> 00:00:58.820
Start at the ones: six plus seven makes thirteen, so exchange ten ones for one ten.

00:00:59.470 --> 00:01:03.991
Eight tens plus five tens plus the exchanged ten makes fourteen tens.

00:01:04.211 --> 00:01:06.009
Continue the regrouping.

00:01:06.229 --> 00:01:10.464
Seven hundreds plus four hundreds plus one hundred makes twelve hundreds.

00:01:10.684 --> 00:01:14.464
The final total is four thousand two hundred and forty-three.

00:01:15.114 --> 00:01:20.569
Now subtract twenty-seven thousand six hundred and eighty-four from fifty-two thousand.

00:01:20.789 --> 00:01:27.289
Across the zeros, exchange one thousand for ten hundreds, then exchange one hundred and one ten as needed.

00:01:27.939 --> 00:01:34.939
Subtract each place after regrouping: six ones, one ten, three hundreds, four thousands and two ten-thousands.

00:01:35.159 --> 00:01:38.785
The difference is twenty-four thousand three hundred and sixteen.

00:01:39.005 --> 00:01:40.599
Add it back to check.

00:01:41.249 --> 00:01:44.085
Regrouping does not create extra value.

00:01:44.305 --> 00:01:49.134
When a zero is involved, exchange from a larger place and adjust that place too.

00:01:49.354 --> 00:01:52.953
Our regrouped parts must still add to fifty-two thousand.

00:01:53.173 --> 00:01:56.255
Checking the total keeps every exchange honest.

00:01:56.905 --> 00:02:00.847
What is four hundred and six minus one hundred and seventy-eight?

00:02:04.847 --> 00:02:06.789
Regroup across the zero.

00:02:07.009 --> 00:02:13.332
Sixteen ones minus eight is eight, nine tens minus seven is two, and three hundreds minus one is two.

00:02:13.552 --> 00:02:16.374
The answer is two hundred and twenty-eight.

00:02:17.024 --> 00:02:21.714
Align place values, regroup without changing the total, and work systematically.

00:02:21.934 --> 00:02:26.321
A zero is a placeholder, so exchanges may cross more than one column.

00:02:26.541 --> 00:02:28.949
Use addition to check subtraction.

00:02:29.169 --> 00:02:32.327
Now choose a strategy and explain why it works.
